    lemma={'key':'complete-hs-tail','namespace':'analysis.operator_bounds','logical_name':'operator-norm-hilbert-schmidt-complete-tail-completion','kind':'lemma','title':'Operator norm and Hilbert-Schmidt tail: Cauchy-Schwarz block completion','statement':'Elementary inequality; proof unaudited. Let T be a bounded linear operator on a Hilbert space H and P an orthogonal projection on H. Let lambda,tau>=0. Assume T-PTP is Hilbert-Schmidt. '+completion+' For a kernel on [0,infinity)^2 with P multiplication by the indicator of [0,L], tau must bound the squared-kernel integral over the entire complement of [0,L]^2: both cross rectangles as well as the outside corner. No positivity, positive semidefiniteness or self-adjointness assumption on T is needed.','proof_text':'For unit f,g set s=||Pf|| ||Pg||. The Hilbert-Schmidt orthogonal projection of the rank-one operator f g* onto P-to-P operators is Pf (Pg)*, of squared Hilbert-Schmidt norm s^2. Its orthogonal remainder has squared norm 1-s^2. Hence |<f,Tg>|<=lambda s+sqrt(tau)sqrt(1-s^2)<=sqrt(lambda^2+tau) by Hilbert-Schmidt and two-dimensional Cauchy-Schwarz. Take the supremum over unit f,g. This is an elementary completion lemma, not a claim of novelty.','assumptions':['T bounded on H','P an orthogonal projection','lambda,tau>=0','T-PTP Hilbert-Schmidt with its ENTIRE squared norm <=tau','Status: T039-C004 v2, proof (unaudited)'],'domain':'operator norm certificates','source':{'source_id':'owner-work:w681:T039-C004:v2','url':'~/brain_workers/w681/T039/proofs/BLOCK_COMPLETION.md','revision':at,'license':'owner-own-work (elementary proof; audit pending)','excerpt':None}}
